SOUNDDVR MIDI SEQUENCER driver-DS + song-seg rebase (asm 0xb5d / 0xc39 / 0xbf7 / 0xcf3, verified vs
re_out/fist_snd_image.bin) -- the FINAL wiring that makes the menu music actually PLAY.

Patch 350 registers the MAINMENU.MS3 KGF'91 song into the DRIVER data seg (DAT_0000_0831<<4): sets
[ds:0x6]=song seg, [ds:0xc]=cursor (0x30 = MIDI stream start), [ds:0xe]=0xffff (playing), [ds:0x14]=1.
Patch 358 rebased the per-tick advance 0a28 which, when [ds:0xe]!=0, calls the sequencer 0c39.  But
0c39 (sequencer) and 0b5d (MIDI event reader) were left with Ghidra's ENGINE-DGROUP model:
  * every driver-DS field read as _DAT_1000_cNN (linear 0x1c000+0xNN) instead of the driver data seg;
  * the FAR song pointer es:[bx] (es=[ds:0x6] song seg, bx=[ds:0xc] cursor) folded into ONE near
    pointer _DAT_1000_c00c -> the reader streamed the wrong segment (engine DGROUP, ==0);
  * 0b5d's 14-bit variable-length delta decode (asm 0xbdc-0xbed) was dropped (it only "skipped 1-2
    bytes" and never returned DX) -> no event timing.
Runtime-proven: [ds:0x6/0xc/0xe/0x14] were correctly set (song 0x4c24, cursor 0x30, playing 0xffff)
yet the cursor never advanced and only 2 key-ons fired over 78 s -- because 0c39 decremented
_DAT_1000_c014 (engine DGROUP, ==0) -> 0xffff -> "!=0" -> returned every tick, never fetching.

This patch reconstructs 0b5d, 0c39 (incl. the 0xbf7 song-end/loop tail = jmp 0xb10) and 0cf3
(program-change) 1:1 from the asm, all based at the driver data seg.  0b5d's multi-register output
(AH note / CH channel-or-0xff / CL velocity / DX delta -- an x86 multi-return the __allregs single
return cannot express) is threaded to the 0c39 note-dispatch loop via new g_snd_ev_* file globals.
The 0b10 song-init parse is factored into a shared static helper snd_song_reparse() so the song-end
loop tail re-registers the song identically to 0af4's initial register.

Chain now closed: 0a28 (per tick) -> 0c39 (decw delay; on 0 -> 0b5d fetch) -> 0b5d (read es:bx MIDI
event, advance cursor, decode delta) -> per note: 0cfb instrument + 0aa7 key-on -> device-3 method
vectors 10a6 (A0/B0 fnum from cs:0x9dd) / 10e3 (key + velocity) / 0f99 (FM patch) -> 0f21 OPL out.

Reached only under FIST_SB/FIST_OPL (device 3 selected + c510 populated via the FIST_SB-gated 014e
section install); the default boot never enters here -> the 26 video flows stay byte-identical.

